course: dictionary
lesson: 294
title: Words for funny
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Amusing is a useful word when you want to say that something made you smile or laugh. It is a gentler word than funny, and it can also mean pleasant and entertaining. Read this: «Some of the younger and livelier animals whispered to each other that things were not so amusing as they used to be in the good old days.»
explain: The clues are whispered, not so amusing as they used to be, and the good old days. The animals are saying that things were less fun and less entertaining than before. So amusing means funny or entertaining here, not sad or loud.
explain: Amusing comes from the verb amuse, which means to make someone smile, laugh or keep them happy. When you meet a new word, try your meaning in the sentence. If «funny» or «entertaining» still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
fact: Amusing means funny in a gentle way that makes you smile or laugh.
fact: Amusing can also mean pleasant and entertaining, keeping you happy for a while.
fact: Amusing is an adjective: more amusing, most amusing.
fact: Amusing comes from the verb amuse, so amuse and amused are in the same family.
fact: Useful phrases: «find it amusing», «an amusing story», «mildly amusing».
exercise: «Some of the younger and livelier animals whispered to each other that things were not so amusing as they used to be in the good old days.» What does amusing mean here? | Sad and lonely | *Funny or entertaining | Very loud | Dangerous
exercise: Lily says, «I find this story amusing.» What does she mean? | She is too tired to read it | She is angry with the story | *She thinks the story is funny or entertaining | She has never heard the story before
exercise: Which word could replace amusing in «an amusing story»? | heavy | sleepy | *funny | sad
test: Why might a writer choose amusing instead of funny? | *It sounds gentler and can show that something is pleasant as well as funny | It means something completely different from funny | It means very sad | It is always the longest word in a sentence
test: Which sentence uses amusing correctly? | The dark cave was amusing and scary | He was amusing, so he fell asleep | The rain was amusing, cold and wet all day | *The clown's silly hat made the children laugh, and they found it amusing
exam: Mia says amusing means boring. Is she right? | Yes, boring is the opposite of amusing | *No, amusing means funny or entertaining | Yes, it means tired and sleepy | Only in the good old days
